**Reused evidence**
- `REUSE_JSON: {"evidence_ids":["E0001"],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.2","3B.4","3B.5","3B.10"]}`
- The constitution source is reused only for ruler authority, command over coercive institutions, and baseline attribution. It is not evidence of restraint by itself.

**New evidence**
- Khamenei’s first response to the Mahsa Amini crisis backed the security forces, blamed enemies, and reframed the protests as disorder rather than a rights claim.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran’s Khamenei backs police over Mahsa Amini protests, may signal tougher crackdown","publisher":"Reuters via Euronews","publication_date":"2022-10-04","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/10/04/iran-women-khamenei","claim":"Khamenei gave full backing to security forces, said Amini’s death was a bitter incident, and portrayed the protests as planned by Iran’s enemies.","locator":"Reuters lead paragraph and quoted speech summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire with direct quotation from Khamenei's first public remarks on the unrest.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 protest period.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Khamenei speech and public posture.","contrary_evidence":["He also said Amini’s death 'deeply broke my heart'.","This is rhetoric and backing, not a documented operational order."],"lenses":["3B.3","3B.6","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- Amnesty documented lethal force, birdshot, and beatings against largely peaceful protesters in the first days after Amini’s death.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran: Deadly crackdown on protests against Mahsa Amini’s death in custody needs urgent global action","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-09-21","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/09/iran-deadly-crackdown-on-protests-against-mahsa-aminis-death-in-custody-needs-urgent-global-action/","claim":"Amnesty said Iranian security forces were violently quashing largely peaceful protests and using birdshot, metal pellets, tear gas, water cannon, and batons; at least eight people were dead and hundreds injured.","locator":"Opening paragraphs and 'Shooting to kill and harm' section","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous rights investigation based on reviewed evidence and eyewitness accounts.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Immediate 2022 protest period.","ruler_attribution":"State security forces under Khamenei’s supreme authority.","contrary_evidence":["The report is advocacy-based and does not by itself prove a direct order from Khamenei.","It acknowledges some protesters engaged in stone-throwing, which does not justify the force used."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.8","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- Amnesty’s follow-up showed escalation to live ammunition, a nationwide internet blackout, and deliberate intimidation of protesters.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran: World must take meaningful action against bloody crackdown as death toll rises","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-09-23","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/09/iran-world-must-take-meaningful-action-against-bloody-crackdown-as-death-toll-rises/","claim":"Amnesty reported deliberate and unlawful live-fire use against protesters across 20 cities and 10 provinces, with the death toll at least 30 and a deliberate internet blackout limiting reporting.","locator":"Opening paragraphs","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous field-based rights reporting with specific casualty and tactics claims.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"State security response under Khamenei’s authority.","contrary_evidence":["The report is based on collected evidence rather than government records.","It documents protester violence as the object of repression, not proof of a single command chain."],"lenses":["3B.5","3B.8","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- Leaked orders obtained by Amnesty pointed to top-level instructions to suppress the protests brutally.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran: Leaked documents reveal top-level orders to armed forces to ‘mercilessly confront’ protesters","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-09-30","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/09/iran-leaked-documents-reveal-top-level-orders-to-armed-forces-to-mercilessly-confront-protesters/","claim":"Amnesty said leaked official documents showed the armed forces' highest body ordered commanders to 'severely confront' protesters and a provincial commander ordered forces to confront them 'mercilessly' even causing deaths.","locator":"Opening paragraphs and leaked-document summary","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"The claim rests on leaked documents analyzed by Amnesty; it is stronger than pure witness testimony but still indirect on provenance.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022, during the core crackdown phase.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional order within Iran’s coercive chain under Khamenei’s overall control; not a personal transcript from him.","contrary_evidence":["The documents are not publicly authenticated by the Iranian government.","They show institutional intent, not a direct on-record Khamenei command."],"lenses":["3B.2","3B.4","3B.5","3B.6","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- HRW documented lethal force in 13 cities and described a concerted government effort to crush dissent.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran: Security Forces Fire On, Kill Protesters","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-10-05","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/10/05/iran-security-forces-fire-kill-protesters","claim":"HRW said security forces used shotguns, assault rifles, and handguns against largely peaceful protesters in 13 cities, killing and injuring hundreds.","locator":"News release body and video-analysis paragraph","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent human-rights analysis with video verification and witness interviews.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Security-force conduct under Khamenei’s national authority.","contrary_evidence":["HRW is not a state fact-finder and does not assign personal orders to Khamenei.","It documents state force, not every local incident."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.2","3B.8","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- Reuters reported Khamenei’s characterization of the unrest as enemy-designed riots.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran's Khamenei calls anti-government protests 'scattered riots' designed by the enemy","publisher":"Reuters via Euronews","publication_date":"2022-10-12","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/10/13/iran-women-khamenei","claim":"Khamenei called the protests 'scattered riots' and said they were the design of the enemy against the Iranian nation.","locator":"Reuters paragraph quoting Tasnim-reported remarks","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire quoting Khamenei through a semi-official outlet.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the protest wave.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Khamenei rhetoric.","contrary_evidence":["The same report notes the protests were sparked by Mahsa Amini’s death in custody.","The source is one step removed through Tasnim and Reuters."],"lenses":["3B.3","3B.6","3B.9"]}
- The UN human-rights office reported violent treatment of women, live ammunition against protesters, and arrests shortly after Amini’s death.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Mahsa Amini: Acting UN human rights chief urges impartial probe into death in Iran","publisher":"OHCHR","publication_date":"2022-09-20","url":"https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2022/09/mahsa-amini-acting-un-human-rights-chief-urges-impartial-probe-death-iran","claim":"OHCHR said there were verified videos of violent treatment of women, and that security forces had reportedly responded to protests with live ammunition, pellet guns, tear gas, arrests, and disproportionate force.","locator":"Final three paragraphs before 'ENDS'","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UN human-rights statement released contemporaneously with the events.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Immediate 2022 crisis period.","ruler_attribution":"State response under Khamenei’s authority.","contrary_evidence":["The UN office reports allegations and verified videos, not a completed judicial finding.","It does not identify Khamenei as the person who ordered each act."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.7","3B.8","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- OHCHR’s communication log captured allegations of torture, sexual violence, extrajudicial executions, unlawful killings, and internet disruption.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Communication report: IRN 23/2022","publisher":"OHCHR Special Procedures","publication_date":"2022-10-20","url":"https://spcommreports.ohchr.org/TmSearch/RelCom?code=IRN+23%2F2022","claim":"OHCHR recorded allegations of ongoing excessive and lethal force by Iranian security forces, including live ammunition, sexual and gender-based violence, arbitrary arrests, torture, extrajudicial executions, unlawful killings, and internet disruption.","locator":"Summary column for IRN 23/2022","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UN special-procedures record summarizing information received from a joint allegation communication.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"State security conduct under the national leadership chain.","contrary_evidence":["This is an allegation/communication record, not a final adjudication.","The record does not isolate every act to Khamenei personally."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.2","3B.5","3B.8","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- NetBlocks confirmed near-total internet disruption in parts of Iran and a nationwide platform restriction sequence during the protests.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Internet disrupted in Iran amid protests over death of Mahsa Amini","publisher":"NetBlocks","publication_date":"2022-09-19","url":"https://netblocks.org/reports/internet-disrupted-in-iran-amid-protests-over-death-of-mahsa-amini-X8qVEwAD","claim":"NetBlocks confirmed a near-total disruption to internet service in parts of Kurdistan province, with national restrictions on Instagram and WhatsApp and a nation-scale mobile-network shutdown soon after.","locator":"Opening paragraphs and status updates quoted in the report","source_type":"technical monitoring","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent network measurement organization with timestamped connectivity analysis.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year and at protest onset.","ruler_attribution":"Shutdowns are state actions under Khamenei’s system, though not individually attributed to him by NetBlocks.","contrary_evidence":["Connectivity data show effects, not motive or a named order.","The report does not prove the shutdown was ordered by Khamenei personally."],"lenses":["3B.5","3B.8","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- Amnesty documented the lethal crackdown in Zahedan and the disproportionate harm to Baluchi civilians, including children.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran: At least 82 Baluchi protesters and bystanders killed in bloody crackdown","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-10-06","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/10/iran-at-least-82-baluchi-protesters-and-bystanders-killed-in-bloody-crackdown/","claim":"Amnesty said Iranian security forces unlawfully killed at least 66 people and injured hundreds in Zahedan on 30 September, later adding 16 more deaths, with victims including children and bystanders.","locator":"Opening paragraphs","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous documented-account report with named victims, witness testimony, and video/image analysis.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Security-force conduct in a minority region under Khamenei’s national authority.","contrary_evidence":["It remains a rights-group estimate rather than a court finding.","The violence was regionally concentrated, so it does not alone establish nationwide uniformity."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.7","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- Amnesty said the authorities sought death sentences in sham trials to intimidate the wider protest movement.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran: Chilling use of the death penalty to further brutally quell popular uprising","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-11-16","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/11/iran-chilling-use-of-the-death-penalty-to-further-brutally-quell-popular-uprising/","claim":"Amnesty said Iranian authorities were seeking the death penalty for at least 21 people in sham trials designed to intimidate protesters and deter others from joining the uprising.","locator":"Opening paragraphs","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous legal-and-human-rights reporting based on case tracking and court proceedings.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Judicial and security-system conduct under Khamenei’s authority.","contrary_evidence":["The report focuses on legal proceedings rather than on street violence.","It does not by itself prove a direct Khamenei order."],"lenses":["3B.4","3B.5","3B.6","3B.8","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- HRW reported the authorities had already issued death sentences, used rushed proceedings, and denied access to chosen lawyers.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran: Death Sentences Against Protesters","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-12-13","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/12/13/iran-death-sentences-against-protesters","claim":"HRW said Iranian authorities executed two men after grossly unfair trials and that revolutionary courts had issued at least 11 other protest-related death sentences, with defendants reportedly denied lawyers of their choice.","locator":"News release body and quoted HRW analysis","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent rights monitoring with specific case details and procedural criticisms.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in late 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Judicial conduct under the Supreme Leader’s institutional authority.","contrary_evidence":["HRW is reporting on due process and punishment, not all underlying protest incidents.","The article still leaves direct command responsibility partly indirect."],"lenses":["3B.4","3B.5","3B.8","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- Reuters reported Khamenei praising Basij forces for confronting “rioters,” with the Basij at the forefront of the crackdown.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran's Khamenei praises Basij forces for confronting 'rioters'","publisher":"Reuters via Yahoo News / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-11-26","url":"https://www.yahoo.com/news/irans-khamenei-praises-basij-forces-for-confronting-rioters-072742042.html","claim":"Khamenei praised the Basij militia for sacrificing their lives in what he called riots, while the Basij were described as being at the forefront of the crackdown.","locator":"Reuters opening paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire with direct attribution, but syndicated through Yahoo rather than the Reuters site itself.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Khamenei endorsement of the aligned force.","contrary_evidence":["The report is about rhetoric and praise, not a written operational order.","It does not establish that the Basij’s every act was personally directed by him."],"lenses":["3B.2","3B.3","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- Access Now’s 2022 shutdown report shows Iran used repeated shutdowns during protests as a tactic of control and cover for abuses.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Weapons of control, shields of impunity: Internet shutdowns in 2022","publisher":"Access Now","publication_date":"2023-02-28","url":"https://www.accessnow.org/internet-shutdowns-2022/","claim":"Access Now said Iran imposed 18 internet shutdowns in 2022, most during protests, and described shutdowns as a weapon of control that often shielded human-rights abuses.","locator":"Key findings and Iran-specific paragraphs","source_type":"NGO/technical monitoring","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent global shutdown-tracking report with country-level counts and thematic analysis.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective but directly about 2022.","ruler_attribution":"State action under Khamenei’s system and protest-response chain.","contrary_evidence":["This is a 2023 synthesis of 2022 events, not a contemporaneous 2022 document.","It documents pattern and context more than individual orders."],"lenses":["3B.5","3B.6","3B.8","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- The UN Human Rights Council created a fact-finding mission because hundreds were killed, minorities were disproportionately affected, and thousands were arrested.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Human Rights Council establishes fact-finding mission to investigate alleged human rights violations in Iran related to the protests that began on 16 September 2022","publisher":"UN Office at Geneva","publication_date":"2022-11-24","url":"https://www.ungeneva.org/en/news-media/meeting-summary/2022/11/afternoon-human-rights-council-establishes-fact-finding-mission","claim":"The Council said the crackdown on peaceful protests had resulted in the death of hundreds of people, including dozens of children, a disproportionate number of minorities, and the arrest of thousands, and it created an independent fact-finding mission.","locator":"Opening summary and resolution description","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UN resolution summary from the meeting that created the mission.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late 2022 and directly about the 2022 protests.","ruler_attribution":"State repression under Khamenei’s authority.","contrary_evidence":["This is a mandate/summary, not the final mission report.","The text is institutional and does not name Khamenei as the operational author of each abuse."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.4","3B.7","3B.10"]}
- The 2024 UN committee report confirms the pattern against minorities, including extrajudicial killings, torture, rape, arbitrary detention, racial profiling, and internet shutdowns, and says there was no independent mechanism for redress.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Right to freedom of peaceful assembly and association in the aftermath of the protests of November 2019, July 2021 and September 2022","publisher":"UN Committee report via OHCHR docstore","publication_date":"2024-04-04","url":"https://docstore.ohchr.org/SelfServices/FilesHandler.ashx?enc=ebBH8prNo22hk1tylgg%2FiBe%2FE8fgTmM1abRF1ZNfYW32Dg%2Bf6YrVDCMg65%2F7fqGRsoEfANCUa%2FE0GZyn8xXUpY7St3j%2Be1ciE8cUik%2B8af8%3D","claim":"The committee reported grave abuses against minority protesters, including disproportionate use of force, extrajudicial killings, torture, rape, arbitrary detention, racial profiling, internet shutdowns, and a lack of any independent mechanism for investigation and redress.","locator":"Paragraph 28(a) and 28(f)","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UN treaty-body text summarizing the persistent pattern and the accountability gap.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective, but directly about the September 2022 protest aftermath.","ruler_attribution":"State security and accountability failure under Khamenei’s authority.","contrary_evidence":["This is a later committee assessment rather than a contemporaneous 2022 field report.","It focuses on assembly and minority-protest violations rather than the entire domestic-safety picture."],"lenses":["3B.4","3B.7","3B.8","3B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
- I reviewed roughly 30 distinct documents across Amnesty, HRW, OHCHR, UN Geneva, NetBlocks, Access Now, Reuters wires, Freedom House, and a few Persian-language/state-aligned outlets.
- I kept sources that added materially different facts: Khamenei’s own rhetoric, security-force tactics, leaked orders, internet shutdowns, lethal-force documentation, minority-specific harms, and failed accountability.
- I rejected duplicated syndications of the same Reuters item when they added no new claim.
- I rejected broad 2023-2026 retrospectives that were not directly about the 2022 crackdown, except where they summarized the 2022 evidence base or accountability gap.
- I rejected generic country profiles when the local prior already covered the static rights baseline and the profile added no new ruler-attributed domestic-safety claim.
- I rejected pure protest-description articles that did not specify force, detention, incitement, or remedy.
- I avoided padding with school-poisoning material because it is mostly 2023 and would pull the dossier away from the 2022 target year.

**Remaining gaps**
- Direct, personal Khamenei orders for specific street-level abuses are still not public; attribution is strong at the system level but indirect at the action level.
- Internal detention, interrogation, and prison chain-of-command evidence is still sparse in public 2022 material.
- There is no clean public record of meaningful accountability or remedy in 2022, which itself is evidence of impunity, but more primary judicial material would sharpen that point.
- If you want, the next useful search would be Persian-language official speeches and judiciary documents for tighter attribution on 3B.2/3B.4/3B.5, but the current set is already enough to show a severe, systematic repression pattern rather than isolated misconduct.
